  "Question": "The larger of two consecutive odd integers is three times the smaller. What is their sum?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(12\\)",
    "D": "\\(16\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Consecutive odd integers differ by \\(2\\). Since the larger integer is three times the smaller, subtracting the smaller from the larger leaves twice the smaller. Therefore the smaller integer is\n\\[\n2\\div(3-1)=1.\n\\]\nThe larger is \\(3\\), and \\(1\\) and \\(3\\) are indeed consecutive odd integers. Their sum is \\(1+3=4\\), choice A.",
